# Wiki Maintainer Schema

This file defines how the LLM wiki in this repository is structured and maintained.
It follows the [LLM Wiki pattern](https://gist.github.com/karpathy/442a6bf555914893e9891c11519de94f).

## Layers

1. **Raw sources** — immutable inputs the wiki is derived from (other repos, exports, notes).
2. **Wiki (`wiki/`)** — LLM-maintained markdown pages with cross-links.
3. **Schema (this file)** — conventions the maintainer must follow on every ingest.

## Directory layout

```
wiki/
├── AGENTS.md          # this schema
├── index.md           # catalog of all wiki pages
├── log.md             # append-only ingest/query/lint timeline
├── overview.md        # high-level synthesis (optional)
├── summaries/         # one page per ingested source/document
├── concepts/          # cross-cutting topics and synthesized knowledge
└── entities/          # services, systems, teams, customers, components
```

## Page types

| Type | Location | When to create | When to update |
|------|----------|----------------|----------------|
| summary | `wiki/summaries/` | New source ingested | Source materially changes |
| concept | `wiki/concepts/` | New cross-cutting topic emerges | Topic behavior or scope changes |
| entity | `wiki/entities/` | New distinct service/system/team | Attributes, ownership, or interfaces change |

**Heuristic:** create a new page for a distinct entity/concept you would link to from elsewhere; edit in place for attribute updates.

## Frontmatter (required on summary, concept, entity pages)

```yaml
---
type: summary | concept | entity
title: Human-readable title
description: One-line summary
tags: [tag1, tag2]
timestamp: 2026-07-11
sources:
  - org/repo@commit
---
```

## Cross-linking

- Use Obsidian-style wikilinks: `[[concepts/payments]]`, `[[entities/api-gateway]]`
- When updating a page, also update pages that link to it if their claims are affected
- Avoid orphan pages; ensure `wiki/index.md` lists every page

## Ingest workflow (automated)

When a source repository changes on `main`:

1. Read the commit diff and determine relevance (API, infra, config, engineer/customer-impacting refactors).
2. Update affected `summaries/`, `concepts/`, and `entities/` pages.
3. Refresh `wiki/index.md` with links and one-line descriptions.
4. Append an entry to `wiki/log.md`:
   `## [YYYY-MM-DD] ingest | org/repo@sha | short summary`

## Relevance bar

Update the wiki when changes affect:

- Public or internal APIs, contracts, schemas, endpoints
- Infrastructure, deployment, configuration, environment variables
- Architecture or runtime behavior engineers or customers rely on
- Internal refactors that change how systems work

Skip updates for formatting-only edits, test-only changes, and dependency bumps with no behavior change.

## Lint (manual / scheduled)

Periodically check for:

- Missing frontmatter fields
- Stale pages contradicted by newer sources
- Orphan pages with no inbound links
- Coverage gaps (concepts mentioned but lacking a page)
- Overview drift (`overview.md` lagging behind recent ingests)

## Naming

- Filenames: lowercase kebab-case (`payment-retries.md`)
- Titles: Title Case in frontmatter
- Prefer fewer, denser pages over many thin duplicates
